The following termcap entries generate the necessary info
to use adds 3a terminals.  Note that an adds 3a+ terminal
is identical to the adm3a+ (in operation at least) and the
termcap entry for the latter may be used.  Both entries
have been  given for completeness.

----------

la|adm3a|3a|lsi adm3a:\
	:am:bs:cm=\E=%+ %+ :cl=1^Z:co#80:ho=^^:li#24:ma=^K^P:nd=^L:up=^K:
lb|adm3a+|3a+:cd=\EY:ce=\ET:kl=^H:kd=^J:ku=^K:kr=^L:kh=^^:tc=adm3a:
# note: an adds 3a is different from an adm3a
# but an adds3a+ is the same as adm's version of the 3a+.
lc|adds3a:\
	:am:bs:cm=\EY%+ %+ :cl=^L:co#80:ho=\EY  :li#24:ma=^Z^P:nd=^F:up=^Z:\
	:kl=^U:kd=^J:ku=^Z:kr=^F:cd=\Ek:ce=\EK:

Note: lc was chosen as the two letter code for no other reason
      than it followed in sequence with the other adm entries.
      Does anyone know why la and lb were chosen for adm, were
      is the significance?

